# OneDrive needs one value from you: the application (client) id of an Entra app
# registration. Registering an app is free, and a single-page application has no
# secret — the id is public by design.
#
#   Entra admin centre → App registrations → New registration
#     Supported account types: personal Microsoft accounts + work/school (multitenant)
#     Platform: Single-page application
#     Redirect URI: http://localhost:5173/            (dev)
#                   https://<your-host>/              (built site)
#     API permissions (delegated): Files.ReadWrite, User.Read
#
# Copy the Application (client) id below and save this file as `.env.local`.
# Leaving it empty is fine: this build ships with its own registration, so anyone can
# connect OneDrive without creating an Entra app. Anything here wins over that one,
# and so does an id typed into the hub (Right-click the account line → the setup asks).
#
# These are build-time values: `npm run build` inlines them into dist/assets/*.js,
# so a static host needs no server. On CI (GitHub Actions → Cloudflare Pages) pass
# them to the build step from a repository variable named VITE_MS_CLIENT_ID.

VITE_MS_CLIENT_ID=

# `common` covers personal and work/school accounts; set a tenant id to pin one.
# A registration that allows only your organisation cannot be reached through `common`
# ("unauthorized_client ... not enabled for consumers"): put its tenant here, or in the
# hub's setup dialog, which also takes the id at runtime.
VITE_MS_TENANT=common
